From d221d7645d354c029c372cbec401d3406724568f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 06:14:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 103/105] hir: associated type bindings with generic arguments
 (`Tr<Assoc<T> = X>`)

hybrid-array 0.4.14 (just 1.58.0, via digest 0.11) puts
`U: ArraySize<ArrayType<T> = [T; N]>` on most of its impls (`ArrayType<T>` is
a GAT):

    BUG: src/hir/from_ast.cpp:853: TODO: get_aty_node - Handle ATYs with args

Upstream 14f262d6 added `aty_params` to `TraitPath::AtyEqual`/`AtyBound`, and
a few consumers already pass them on (`equate_types_assoc`, trait-impl
`ImplRef::get_type`, the projection for `Assoc<..>: Bound`). Lowering still
refused any arguments, though, and most places that copy, index or look up
a binding ignored them. This finishes the job:

- from_ast: lower the arguments instead of hitting the TODO.
- Keep them when a binding is monomorphised (`monomorph_tp_aty_equal`, the
  AtyBound copy), turned into an ImplRef (static `find_impl`, the ATY-bound
  path of `find_trait_impls_bound`), inherited from a supertrait (bind
  `fill_type_aliases`) or rebuilt for a trait object.
- Visit them in HIR::Visitor, ExprVisitorDef and the typeck TyVisitor, so the
  binding passes and the monomorph-needed checks see types written there.
- A binding applies only to a projection with the same arguments (types and
  values; lifetimes are ignored as `PathParams ==` does):
  - the bound-equality index (`prep_indexes`) is keyed by the projection with
    its arguments;
  - `ImplRef::get_type` for bounds compares them, through typeck's ivars when
    given (new optional argument; it asserted before);
  - the name lookups in the cached bounds, bounds on associated types, their
    supertraits and `impl Trait` check them;
  - `check_associated` passes the rule's arguments to `get_type` (it passed
    `{}`, which broke a GAT impl whose type uses the GAT's own parameter).
  Under `U: ArraySize<ArrayType<T> = [T; N]>`, `ArrayType<T>` is `[T; N]` and
  `ArrayType<u8>` stays opaque.
- A binding under `for<'a>` that names the HRL in its own arguments
  (`for<'a> Lend<Item<'a> = &'a u32>`) takes the projection's lifetime.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
